Third-party data
----------------

NYC 311 Service Requests (dataset erm2-nwe9), City of New York, NYC Open Data:
https://data.cityofnewyork.us/Social-Services/311-Service-Requests-from-2010-to-Present/erm2-nwe9

This repository redistributes only derived aggregates: monthly borough x complaint-type
counts (`data/snapshots/`) and daily counts for 21 selected series (`data/silver/`).
No individual service-request record, address or free text is included. NYC Open Data
is published for public use under the City's Terms of Use:
https://www.nyc.gov/main/terms-of-use
This is an independent project with no affiliation with, or endorsement by, the City of
New York.

Third-party software
--------------------

The Prophet adapter adapts parts of prophet-forecasting-mlops
(https://github.com/soulipaco/prophet-forecasting-mlops, commit b2538be, MIT License,
Copyright (c) 2026 Onur Uslu); see docs/adr/prophet_adapter.md.

Prophet, Optuna, the Databricks SDK and other dependencies are used under their own
licences as resolved in uv.lock. Databricks `ai_forecast` is a managed Databricks SQL
function; no Databricks model weights or code are redistributed here.
